189 in the record book of the Daytona 500.

01:18:47.790 --> 01:18:50.470
Bobby Labonte moves to the outside now of Jeremy Mayfield.

01:18:50.590 --> 01:18:53.050
They'll go side-by-side for second down the short tube.

01:18:53.170 --> 01:18:57.170
Bobby made a run down the back straightaway and got the third spot away from Rusty Wallace.

01:18:57.330 --> 01:18:59.630
Now he's racing side-by-side with Mayfield for second.

01:18:59.630 --> 01:18:59.970
And here comes.

01:19:00.060 --> 01:19:01.960
Gordon, his inside. Earnhardt over the block.

01:19:02.080 --> 01:19:04.140
Bumper tag going on at 190 miles

01:19:04.140 --> 01:19:06.020
an hour. They're in one. Mayfield goes to the

01:19:06.020 --> 01:19:08.180
inside now. Tries to pull up alongside Earnhardt.

01:19:08.260 --> 01:19:10.100
Earnhardt gets away. It'll be Mayfield

01:19:10.100 --> 01:19:12.240
and Gordon. They'll race for the second spot.

01:19:12.640 --> 01:19:13.980
Earnhardt gets two car lengths

01:19:13.980 --> 01:19:15.820
out in front. Still Ford and Chevy

01:19:15.820 --> 01:19:18.120
side by side for second. Behind them

01:19:18.120 --> 01:19:20.080
momentarily three wide as Rusty

01:19:20.080 --> 01:19:22.060
Wallace inside. Skinner in the middle. Bobby

01:19:22.060 --> 01:19:24.140
Labonte outside now. Funnels back to double

01:19:24.140 --> 01:19:25.960
wide. Racing for the second spot.

01:19:26.280 --> 01:19:27.920
Mayfield gets strapped and out for Wallace

01:19:27.920 --> 01:19:29.980
to push him up into the second spot. Mayfield

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:31.940
dives down low, gets drafting help from

01:19:31.940 --> 01:19:33.800
Rusty Wallace, retakes second, now

01:19:33.800 --> 01:19:35.800
Wallace dives down to the inside of Gordon,

01:19:35.900 --> 01:19:37.640
the battle is on for third, off four.

01:19:37.800 --> 01:19:39.960
Better get your best hold and hang on

01:19:39.960 --> 01:19:42.060
as they work their way back down to the start-finish line,

01:19:42.180 --> 01:19:43.900
laps are winding down to the Daytona 500,

01:19:44.080 --> 01:19:46.020
there will be six to go, Earnhardt still

01:19:46.020 --> 01:19:47.780
hangs onto the lead, Jeremy Mayfield

01:19:47.780 --> 01:19:49.460
rides right behind him, single file,

01:19:49.860 --> 01:19:52.140
third place in jeopardy right now in turn one.

01:19:52.280 --> 01:19:53.880
That is where Jeff Gordon works the outside

01:19:53.880 --> 01:19:55.860
lane, he'll get drafting help from Bobby Labonte

01:19:55.860 --> 01:19:57.740
to the inside there, Rusty Wallace,

01:19:58.080 --> 01:19:59.500
he's trying to make up some ground,

01:19:59.500 --> 01:19:59.780
and...

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:01.800
does. Wallace gets by. Labonte

01:20:01.800 --> 01:20:03.940
moves back to fourth, while Earnhardt

01:20:03.940 --> 01:20:05.800
still leads Jeremy Mayfield. First

01:20:05.800 --> 01:20:07.780
side-by-side battles. Kent Schrader down

01:20:07.780 --> 01:20:09.760
to the inside of Bobby Labonte. That's for the fifth

01:20:09.760 --> 01:20:11.720
spot, while the front four run single file.

01:20:12.200 --> 01:20:13.940
Earnhardt, Mayfield, Gordon,

01:20:14.260 --> 01:20:16.180
Wallace, then side-by-side Schrader

01:20:16.180 --> 01:20:18.020
and Labonte. Schrader with a good shot

01:20:18.020 --> 01:20:19.800
down the back straightaway. Flanks Labonte

01:20:19.800 --> 01:20:21.720
as they go side-by-side for fifth.

01:20:21.880 --> 01:20:23.660
He'll pick up drafting help on the inside.

01:20:23.900 --> 01:20:25.700
Ernie Irvin is there as they race off the turn.

01:20:25.900 --> 01:20:27.820
Down to the start-finish line. Five

01:20:27.820 --> 01:20:29.680
laps to go in the Daytona 500.

01:20:30.280 --> 01:20:34.460
Dale Earnhardt, Jeremy Mayfield, Jeff Gordon, and Rusty Wallace.

01:20:34.460 --> 01:20:37.540
Now single file, the first four, door-to-door for fifth.

01:20:37.700 --> 01:20:40.640
Ken Schrader and Bobby Labonte, they're double wide from there on back,

01:20:40.640 --> 01:20:42.760
but the front four lined up and moving away.

01:20:42.960 --> 01:20:46.500
Everybody waiting to see when the opportunity will present itself for Earnhardt.

01:20:46.600 --> 01:20:49.220
All he can do is wait and see what's going to shape up behind him.

01:20:49.360 --> 01:20:52.060
For now, Jeremy Mayfield tucked right in behind him,

01:20:52.320 --> 01:20:55.360
then third place, Jeff Gordon riding along, also in single file.

01:20:55.520 --> 01:20:58.620
Rusty Wallace in the fourth spot, trying to block an advance from Kent Schrader.

01:20:58.740 --> 01:20:59.980
Schrader got the fifth spot on.

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:01.600
Wallace, but now Wallace blocks.

01:21:01.840 --> 01:21:04.000
They're side-by-side for sixth. Ernie Irvin

01:21:04.000 --> 01:21:05.900
down low. Bobby Labonte up high.

01:21:06.080 --> 01:21:07.860
Still side-by-side as they climb the banking.

01:21:08.000 --> 01:21:09.840
Bobby Labonte gets some help from behind. Jimmy

01:21:09.840 --> 01:21:11.820
Spencer goes up high as well. They'll stay

01:21:11.820 --> 01:21:13.780
side-by-side for sixth off four.

01:21:13.960 --> 01:21:16.040
Still a four-car breakaway at the front of the field.

01:21:16.100 --> 01:21:17.920
You have to wonder what's going through Dale Earnhardt's

01:21:17.920 --> 01:21:19.880
mind. He may be thinking, you know, this is the best

01:21:19.880 --> 01:21:21.840
car I've probably ever had here. Might be the

01:21:21.840 --> 01:21:23.920
last chance in my career I have to win

01:21:23.920 --> 01:21:26.000
the Daytona 500. Gonna be hard

01:21:26.000 --> 01:21:27.920
to take it away from him, Joe Moore, as he works his

01:21:27.920 --> 01:21:29.800
way down to the corner, whoever, if, if

01:21:29.800 --> 01:21:29.980
then

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:31.720
If anybody pulls it off, they will earn it.

01:21:31.860 --> 01:21:34.280
We've seen Dale Earnhardt make that car plenty wide,

01:21:34.280 --> 01:21:35.440
and that's what he's going to have to do

01:21:35.440 --> 01:21:38.240
because he knows he'll try to mount a challenge from behind him.

01:21:38.380 --> 01:21:39.860
Here's the challenge for third, though,

01:21:39.920 --> 01:21:41.780
as Rusty goes after Jeff Gordon.

01:21:41.980 --> 01:21:43.480
Folks, the headlight from out from behind.

01:21:43.660 --> 01:21:44.580
Gordon's Chevrolet.

01:21:44.700 --> 01:21:45.960
Now Rusty down on the inside.

01:21:46.200 --> 01:21:46.940
Now three wide.

01:21:47.080 --> 01:21:48.100
Schrader goes to the outside.

01:21:48.440 --> 01:21:49.480
Now Wallace gets third.

01:21:49.740 --> 01:21:50.700
Schrader comes with him.

01:21:50.980 --> 01:21:52.960
Schrader-Wallace side by side for third spot.

01:21:53.120 --> 01:21:55.240
Third spot under contention in turn number three

01:21:55.240 --> 01:21:56.620
as Wallace digs into the bottom.

01:21:56.780 --> 01:21:57.820
Schrader goes up high.

01:21:57.940 --> 01:21:59.920
The front two breakaway off the fourth turn.

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:02.500
The Courage Award for the day goes to Ken Schrader.

01:22:02.660 --> 01:22:03.960
Driving with a cracked sternum.

01:22:04.060 --> 01:22:07.120
Suffered in a hard crash here Thursday during the 125s.

01:22:07.220 --> 01:22:08.720
Jeff Gordon left out of the draft.

01:22:08.940 --> 01:22:09.980
He's falling back.

01:22:10.220 --> 01:22:11.980
Something wrong with Gordon's car.

01:22:12.120 --> 01:22:14.080
As the field goes by Gordon's car,

01:22:14.100 --> 01:22:16.560
he's falling off the pace down to the tail end of the field

01:22:16.560 --> 01:22:17.880
as the leaders go back to one.

01:22:17.940 --> 01:22:19.160
Everybody storms by.

01:22:19.300 --> 01:22:21.000
Jeff Gordon, he hugs the inside lane.

01:22:21.120 --> 01:22:23.060
The entire field flashes by.

01:22:23.340 --> 01:22:24.540
Earnhardt shows the way.

01:22:24.800 --> 01:22:26.360
Jeremy Mayfield, steal with him.

01:22:26.600 --> 01:22:28.540
The battle now for third off turn two.

01:22:28.540 --> 01:22:29.980
Bobby Labonte takes the out.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:34.680
Outside lane gets up alongside Rusty Wallace, and Rusty has no one to dance with.

01:22:35.060 --> 01:22:36.140
Bobby Labonte goes by.

01:22:36.460 --> 01:22:37.580
Jimmy Spencer goes by.

01:22:37.920 --> 01:22:38.760
Schrader goes by.

01:22:38.900 --> 01:22:41.240
Wallace gets in line, but feels a challenge from Ernie Irvin.

01:22:41.380 --> 01:22:45.020
Bobby Labonte shoots down the back straightaway, slips it up to the outside lane.

01:22:45.180 --> 01:22:47.700
Now the challenge is on for second off turn four.

01:22:48.000 --> 01:22:50.720
Rides his way right up against the wall as they come down to the line.

01:22:51.020 --> 01:22:54.040
Laps are winding down in a hurry in the Daytona 500 now.

01:22:54.180 --> 01:22:58.700
Bobby Labonte gets right behind Earnhardt, sandwiches himself in there in a contention

01:22:58.700 --> 01:22:59.880
to win that $1 million.

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:01.900
bonus in the No Bull 5.

01:23:02.080 --> 01:23:04.160
Can he pull it off? He's working Earnhardt over

01:23:04.160 --> 01:23:06.160
in turn one. Earnhardt shows the way back

01:23:06.160 --> 01:23:08.060
into turn one. Hugging the inside of the racetrack

01:23:08.060 --> 01:23:09.840
with Bobby Levani. A car linked behind him.

01:23:10.160 --> 01:23:11.940
Mayfield rides along in third now.

01:23:12.180 --> 01:23:13.960
Then Ken Schrader in fourth. Fifth

01:23:13.960 --> 01:23:16.120
is Rusty Wallace. The battle is going on

01:23:16.120 --> 01:23:18.260
for the sixth spot. Oh, now trouble off the turn.

01:23:18.540 --> 01:23:20.140
One car slides down to the inside

01:23:20.140 --> 01:23:21.940
at his late speed. He makes contact

01:23:21.940 --> 01:23:23.980
with John Andretti. Both cars spin

01:23:23.980 --> 01:23:25.960
down to the inside of the racetrack as everyone

01:23:25.960 --> 01:23:27.960
else gets away. This is the race for the win

01:23:27.960 --> 01:23:29.980
of the Daytona 500, Fields in three.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:33.660
Earnhardt swings up to the top of Rick Mass, the lap car on the bottom of the racetrack.

01:23:33.860 --> 01:23:38.120
Dale Earnhardt puts on the block. Earnhardt slips off turn four, back to the checkered flag.

01:23:38.360 --> 01:23:41.020
Earnhardt in front of Bobby Labonte, a lap car to the inside.

01:23:41.240 --> 01:23:44.780
Rusty Wallace make that Mayfield and Labonte banging for second to the stripe.

01:23:45.180 --> 01:23:48.140
Dale Earnhardt comes to the white flag and the caution flag,

01:23:48.320 --> 01:23:53.260
and Dale Earnhardt is going to win the Daytona 500 in his 20th try.

01:23:53.720 --> 01:23:55.340
It'll be Earnhardt coming to the stripe,

01:23:55.340 --> 01:23:59.980
Finally eluding the one prize in NASCAR racing that has eluded him the most.

01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:01.620
over his illustrious career.

01:24:02.060 --> 01:24:03.640
Let's go back to turn number two,

01:24:03.780 --> 01:24:06.260
recap the incident that brought out the caution flag

01:24:06.260 --> 01:24:08.920
and set up a white flag finish for the 500.

01:24:09.080 --> 01:24:11.880
It was trouble back in the pack a little ways, Alan.

01:24:12.020 --> 01:24:14.220
Lake Speed and John Andretti made contact

01:24:14.220 --> 01:24:15.520
once they came off the banking.

01:24:15.860 --> 01:24:18.680
Both cars spun down to the inside, out of harm's way.

01:24:18.860 --> 01:24:20.160
Everyone else drove on by.

01:24:20.540 --> 01:24:22.360
Both those cars able to continue as well,

01:24:22.460 --> 01:24:24.660
but it set up the finish of the Daytona 500.

01:24:25.160 --> 01:24:27.180
Dale Earnhardt will be rolling down to victory lane

01:24:27.180 --> 01:24:28.820
and talk about an emotional victory lane.

01:24:28.920 --> 01:24:29.980
I got a feeling we're going to have one.

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:33.940
today. Quickly, let's give you the top five. Earnhardt will win. Bobby Labonte will finish

01:24:33.940 --> 01:24:37.920
second. Running third should be Jeremy Mayfield. Kenny Schrader, what a move he

01:24:37.920 --> 01:24:42.020
made with about five laps to go up there to get himself in contention to win, but he settles for fourth

01:24:42.020 --> 01:24:46.020
and Rusty Wallace make up the top five as they cross the stripe under the checkered flag

01:24:46.020 --> 01:24:49.700
making it official and Dale Earnhardt has won the Daytona 500.

01:24:50.020 --> 01:24:53.860
Left arm out the window, fist clenched high in the air as he takes the

01:24:53.860 --> 01:24:57.920
checkered flag. For Dale Earnhardt, so many times he's come so close here

01:24:57.920 --> 01:24:59.980
We're at Daytona four times, finishing six.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:00.860
Second of the 500.

01:25:01.690 --> 01:25:05.390
Back in 1990, a clear lead less than a mile from victory lane

01:25:05.390 --> 01:25:07.530
when he ran over a piece of bell housing,

01:25:07.670 --> 01:25:10.510
dropped from another car, and cut down a tire in turn number three

01:25:10.510 --> 01:25:13.250
and faded back into the field less than a mile from the finish.

01:25:13.450 --> 01:25:16.330
Today, though, he holds off a frantic late charge

01:25:16.330 --> 01:25:21.460
by Bobby Labonte, Jeremy Mayfield, Jeff Gordon, Ken Schrader, and others,

01:25:21.620 --> 01:25:25.280
and Dale Earnhardt will win the 1998 Daytona 500.

01:25:25.660 --> 01:25:27.540
Victory lane and post-race coverage

01:25:27.540 --> 01:25:29.960
when we come back to the World Center of Racing, Earnhardt.

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:32.080
will be the winner of the Daytona 500.

01:25:32.500 --> 01:25:34.320
And now coming down the pit lane

01:25:34.320 --> 01:25:37.380
will be the champion of the 1998 Daytona 500,

01:25:37.580 --> 01:25:40.260
Dale Earnhardt, all the pit crews, all of them,

01:25:40.590 --> 01:25:42.650
out on pit lane to salute the man

01:25:42.650 --> 01:25:44.550
who has accomplished so much in this sport

01:25:44.550 --> 01:25:46.270
except win its biggest race.

01:25:46.330 --> 01:25:49.780
He doesn't have to answer that question anymore after today.

01:25:50.370 --> 01:25:51.690
We'll go to Victory Lane in a moment

01:25:51.690 --> 01:25:53.410
from the Daytona International Speedway.

01:25:53.570 --> 01:25:54.530
This is MRN Radio.

01:25:54.870 --> 01:25:56.750
We left you a moment ago for the commercial break.

01:25:56.850 --> 01:25:58.670
Dale Earnhardt was at the head end of pit road.

01:25:58.810 --> 01:25:59.970
He hasn't moved about a third.

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:02.060
of the way down it as all of the members

01:26:02.060 --> 01:26:04.140
from all of the pit crews along pit road

01:26:04.140 --> 01:26:05.800
are out giving Earnhardt handshakes

01:26:05.800 --> 01:26:08.100
and high fives as he slowly creeps

01:26:08.100 --> 01:26:09.720
his way toward victory lane

01:26:09.720 --> 01:26:11.800
and his winner's trophy for the

01:26:11.800 --> 01:26:13.460
Daytona 500 victory today.

01:26:13.980 --> 01:26:15.880
Earnhardt beating Bobby Labonte back

01:26:15.880 --> 01:26:17.900
to the stripe when an accident happened midway

01:26:17.900 --> 01:26:19.980
through the field off of turn number two

01:26:19.980 --> 01:26:21.680
as they were coming to the white flag.

01:26:22.260 --> 01:26:23.940
Earnhardt beat Bobby Labonte back to the

01:26:23.940 --> 01:26:25.860
white. Labonte was busy trying to deal with

01:26:25.860 --> 01:26:27.980
Jeremy Mayfield whom he was racing for second.

01:26:28.240 --> 01:26:29.860
The lap car of Rick Mast was down

01:26:29.860 --> 01:26:29.920
of

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:32.360
The inside, that factored in as well, but it didn't matter.

01:26:32.460 --> 01:26:34.700
They weren't going to catch Dale Earnhardt at that point, I don't believe.

01:26:35.000 --> 01:26:38.200
And Earnhardt scores the win in the 1998 Daytona 500.

01:26:38.560 --> 01:26:42.360
It'll be Labonte getting second, Jeremy Mayfield third, Rusty Wallace fourth,

01:26:42.400 --> 01:26:45.700
and Ken Schrader with a gutsy performance to come up with fifth position.

01:26:45.700 --> 01:26:47.840
Let's go down to the 76 gas pumps now

01:26:47.840 --> 01:26:50.140
and hear from some of the other top finishers in the race.

01:26:50.280 --> 01:26:51.180
First with the runner-up.

01:26:51.300 --> 01:26:54.100
Bobby Labonte has just climbed out of the interstate Pontiac,

01:26:54.240 --> 01:26:56.540
and I'll tell you something, the whale of a speed week's obviously.

01:26:56.760 --> 01:26:59.900
But he got back to about seventh there with a couple, three laps to go.

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:02.560
and I said, well, you're finished, and lo and behold, I was wrong.

01:27:02.720 --> 01:27:04.320
Man, I'll tell you what, I thought I was finished, too,

01:27:04.400 --> 01:27:06.120
but Jimmy Spencer helped me out quite a bit,

01:27:06.140 --> 01:27:07.400
and I think he got up in the fence there,

01:27:07.400 --> 01:27:10.410
and, you know, we just had a great week with Interstate Batteries, Pontiac,

01:27:10.550 --> 01:27:12.610
and I'd like to thank everybody that's worked on this car,

01:27:12.730 --> 01:27:15.490
and, you know, those are the guys that put a fast race car underneath me,

01:27:15.490 --> 01:27:18.300
and then, you know, I had a feeling Earnhardt was going to be pretty good here,

01:27:18.400 --> 01:27:21.400
and he usually is, and lo and behold, I couldn't get mine there at the end,

01:27:21.480 --> 01:27:23.960
and I think it was Jeremy and I had a really good race there at the end.

01:27:23.980 --> 01:27:26.620
I couldn't tell if it was Rusty and I, because those cars were painted up too much alike,

01:27:26.620 --> 01:27:29.810
But I knew it was one of those Penske cars, and I've got to thank these guys.

01:27:30.000 --> 01:27:31.820
Interstate grew for just giving me a great car.

01:27:32.040 --> 01:27:34.160
And you and Spencer did work well all week, didn't you?

01:27:34.340 --> 01:27:35.340
Yeah, I mean, we just did.

01:27:35.480 --> 01:27:37.360
For some reason, I couldn't follow him that good,

01:27:37.400 --> 01:27:38.900
but when he got behind me, we took off.

01:27:39.040 --> 01:27:41.980
So, you know, I knew he was going to help me.

01:27:42.120 --> 01:27:44.640
It was the two Penske cars were teammates,

01:27:44.760 --> 01:27:47.740
and then Gordon and the, I mean, Skinner and the three car,

01:27:47.860 --> 01:27:50.000
and then the 24 car was there, and then Spencer,

01:27:50.040 --> 01:27:51.360
and he was helping me out all week long.

01:27:51.500 --> 01:27:53.840
So we worked really good, and he helped me out to get to second.

01:27:54.120 --> 01:27:56.400
So a runner-up tucked away here at Daytona.

01:27:56.540 --> 01:27:58.500
It's on to Rockingham for Bobby Labonte.

01:27:58.640 --> 01:27:59.700
Going to take a knock. Congratulations.

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:02.740
from his teammate Rusty Wallace, veteran Ken Schrader.

01:28:03.140 --> 01:28:04.860
Jeremy, I'll tell you what we were commenting during the commercials.

01:28:05.020 --> 01:28:06.620
You drove one heck of a race.

01:28:06.780 --> 01:28:09.200
Well, it makes it easy for me when you've got a car like I had today.

01:28:09.340 --> 01:28:11.500
The Mobile One Ford was great all day.

01:28:11.660 --> 01:28:13.660
You know, the motor ran good, like I think Larry Wallace.

01:28:13.900 --> 01:28:15.980
And the whole pit crew, you know, everybody done a great job.

01:28:15.980 --> 01:28:18.240
Paul Andrews, Rusty Wallace, Roger Penske,

01:28:18.340 --> 01:28:21.600
everybody that's part of this team played their part today,

01:28:21.680 --> 01:28:22.240
and that's what happened.

01:28:22.380 --> 01:28:23.640
You did your part as well.

01:28:23.780 --> 01:28:25.120
Tell us about those last ten laps.

01:28:25.200 --> 01:28:25.960
It was you and Rusty.

01:28:26.040 --> 01:28:27.160
Looks like you could get a run on him.

01:28:27.240 --> 01:28:28.760
And then Bobby Labonte came in there.

01:28:28.960 --> 01:28:29.840
Describe those for us.

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:31.380
Well, it was a good run, you know,

01:28:31.440 --> 01:28:33.480
and I seen everybody shuffling up back there in the back,

01:28:33.480 --> 01:28:36.460
and I was worried because I knew I couldn't get around any by myself,

01:28:36.500 --> 01:28:39.500
and then Bobby got a good run on us past their 10,

01:28:39.680 --> 01:28:40.780
but we didn't give it to him easy.

01:28:41.160 --> 01:28:43.760
You think you and Rusty had anything for him if you could have stayed together?

01:28:43.920 --> 01:28:44.460
I think so.

01:28:44.540 --> 01:28:45.800
You know, I was sitting there riding.

01:28:46.040 --> 01:28:49.060
You know, Earnhardt was strong all day, and I'm not saying we could beat him,

01:28:49.140 --> 01:28:51.520
but I know we had a good car, and we was going to give it our best shot.

01:28:51.780 --> 01:28:53.520
Well, he gave it one heck of a shot today.

01:28:53.680 --> 01:28:55.180
Jeremy Mayfield comes home third.

01:28:55.710 --> 01:28:58.370
Down in victory lane, Dale Earnhardt has just climbed from his car.

01:28:58.510 --> 01:28:59.830
He's standing on the roof.

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:01.760
of the machine, showering champagne

01:29:01.760 --> 01:29:03.720
everywhere, enjoying his victory in the

01:29:03.720 --> 01:29:05.800
Daytona 500. We will go there

01:29:05.800 --> 01:29:08.180
and get a word with the race winner momentarily.

01:29:08.420 --> 01:29:09.700
First, let's go back to the garage.

01:29:10.160 --> 01:29:11.980
A check of the photo finish camera

01:29:11.980 --> 01:29:13.780
gives Ken Schrader fourth spot

01:29:13.780 --> 01:29:15.900
ahead of Rusty Wallace in fifth, so it'll

01:29:15.900 --> 01:29:17.860
be Schrader fourth. A great

01:29:17.860 --> 01:29:19.900
performance today after starting from the back of the

01:29:19.900 --> 01:29:21.840
field with that cracked sternum. Let's see if we can get

01:29:21.840 --> 01:29:23.920
an update. Let's go down to victory lane and see what's

01:29:23.920 --> 01:29:25.820
going on down there. I'll tell you what, this guy, we're

01:29:25.820 --> 01:29:27.820
going up on the podium right now. He's getting a lot of

01:29:27.820 --> 01:29:29.860
hugs from everybody. He said he's going to

01:29:29.860 --> 01:29:29.980
Thank you.

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:39.300
follow me up here, so we'll just walk up. Dale, 20th time is a charm. Your thoughts? 20 years of

01:29:39.300 --> 01:29:43.480
hard work. I tell you, thank the good Lord for a good day. I tell you, we got a lot of great race

01:29:43.480 --> 01:29:48.300
fans, a lot of people behind me that really all week long, they say, this is your week, this is

01:29:48.300 --> 01:29:52.850
your week. Richard Childress has got one heck of a race team. I'm talking about everybody works

01:29:52.850 --> 01:29:58.240
for Richard Childress from the 31 to three truck. Everybody, all this three team, everybody's worked

01:29:58.240 --> 01:29:59.080
so hard for this.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:02.760
I can't believe we won it in the fashion we did.

01:30:02.840 --> 01:30:05.740
We raced them hard, and, you know, it's just a good race car.

01:30:05.880 --> 01:30:07.140
It says a lot for the team.

01:30:07.140 --> 01:30:08.640
It says a lot for all our sponsors.

01:30:09.310 --> 01:30:11.470
Everybody works so hard as Chevrolet Monte Carlo.

01:30:12.410 --> 01:30:13.270
It is something else.

01:30:13.950 --> 01:30:15.830
After Thursday, did you think this was it?

01:30:16.780 --> 01:30:18.880
Well, I had a good feeling we got a good race car,

01:30:18.960 --> 01:30:22.000
and, you know, that's what's important is have a good race car,

01:30:22.040 --> 01:30:25.980
and we worked awful hard all day long to keep it in position

01:30:25.980 --> 01:30:27.720
and keep it in place to win.

01:30:28.130 --> 01:30:28.570
All right.

01:30:28.670 --> 01:30:29.930
This is the first win in 15.

01:30:30.000 --> 01:30:36.000
nine times. Can you win that championship now? Yeah, that's what we're going to do. We're going

01:30:36.000 --> 01:30:40.860
to go for the championship now. We got a great team. His team will win the championship. Dale

01:30:40.860 --> 01:30:47.440
Earnhardt wins his first Daytona 500. And he's back. He is back. No question about that. His name

01:30:47.440 --> 01:30:52.840
will now go on the Harley Earl Trophy as the winner of the 40th 500. If you looked at that

01:30:52.840 --> 01:30:57.380
trophy, there would be no question that certainly in its modern era, that was the most conspicuous

01:30:57.380 --> 01:30:59.760
absence on it and now they learn heart will

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:03.960
and go along as the winner of the Daytona 500 for 1998.

01:31:04.520 --> 01:31:08.000
Yet it is Earnhardt in victory lane and a great story.

01:31:08.320 --> 01:31:12.000
I mean, the man has just accomplished everything there is to be accomplished in this business

01:31:12.000 --> 01:31:14.460
except win its biggest race, and he's done that now.

01:31:14.600 --> 01:31:19.160
It'd be a shame for Earnhardt to end his career and his name not be on the trophy

01:31:19.160 --> 01:31:21.480
having won the Daytona 500 over the years.

01:31:21.940 --> 01:31:25.320
It wouldn't be, you know, that, as Earnhardt told me one time,

01:31:25.400 --> 01:31:28.220
he said, if I never win the thing, I've had a heck of a run in this business,

01:31:28.240 --> 01:31:29.960
and he has, but it just makes you.

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:32.080
feel good. And I think even whether you're an Earnhardt

01:31:32.080 --> 01:31:33.860
fan or not out there listening or watching today,

01:31:34.160 --> 01:31:36.000
you still got a feel for Dale Earnhardt

01:31:36.000 --> 01:31:37.520
because he deserves to win the 500.

01:31:37.740 --> 01:31:39.920
Like him or not, he has stood for excellence

01:31:39.920 --> 01:31:41.940
behind the wheel in this business for a long

01:31:41.940 --> 01:31:43.860
time and is one of its most accomplished

01:31:43.860 --> 01:31:46.000
drivers ever. And for him to be the winner

01:31:46.000 --> 01:31:47.800
of its greatest race certainly is very

01:31:47.800 --> 01:31:49.760
appropriate. Certainly to start the

01:31:49.760 --> 01:31:51.780
50th year of NASCAR, that's a great way

01:31:51.780 --> 01:31:53.960
to begin the celebration of 50 years of the sport.

01:31:54.120 --> 01:31:55.820
Now for Barney Hall. This is Alan

01:31:55.820 --> 01:31:57.740
Bestwick saying so long from Daytona.

01:31:57.940 --> 01:31:59.640
Dale Earnhardt is in victory lane as

01:31:59.640 --> 01:31:59.980
But what?

01:32:00.000 --> 01:32:01.880
Winning the 40th Daytona 500.
